emscripten: jobs run synchronously in a program linked without threads.

Blocking calls (Lwt_unix file operations, Lwt_io.with_file...) are "jobs"
run by a pool of POSIX threads.  A program linked without threads (no
--threads) cannot start any: lwt_unix_start_job would raise Unix_error
(EOPNOTSUPP, "launch_thread").  They run synchronously instead, as lwt
does when its pool is full.  The stubs are compiled for threads either way
(-pthread): the program decides, when it runs.

--- a/src/unix/lwt_unix_stubs.c
+++ b/src/unix/lwt_unix_stubs.c
@@
   lwt_unix_async_method async_method = Int_val(val_async_method);
   int done = 0;
+
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+  /* ocaml-emcc: no threads, the job runs synchronously */
+  extern int emscripten_has_threading_support(void);
+  if (!emscripten_has_threading_support()) async_method = LWT_UNIX_ASYNC_METHOD_NONE;
+#endif
